        "original_id": "4c343bf2-a00b-5f22-86a4-47ada4b9112b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Othonna, Stangeria eriopus, Othonna capensis\n- Places: Africa, southern Africa, South Africa, Australia\n- Taxa: Asteraceae, sunflower family, cycad, Bowenia, Stangeriaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Othonna is a genus of African plants in the sunflower family.\n- Stangeria eriopus is a cycad endemic to southern Africa.\n- Stangeria eriopus is the only species in the genus Stangeria.\n- Stangeria eriopus is most closely related to the Australian genus Bowenia.\n- Stangeria and Bowenia form the family Stangeriaceae.\n- Othonna capensis, also known as Little Pickles, is a species in the genus Othonna and the family Asteraceae.\n- Othonna capensis is native to South Africa.",
